178 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (Many users are exposed to fraud attempts during everyday financial transactions. These incidents may lead not only to individual financial losses, but also to reputational and operational security risks for service providers. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
179 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (This project developed a data-driven and statistically grounded anomaly detection approach to address the limitations of rule-based systems. The objective was to model users' transaction habits, learn normal behavioral patterns, and detect deviations from those patterns. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
180 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 127 0 R
/E (Both traditional metric-based analysis methods, such as Z-Score and Dynamic Thresholding, and machine learning-based models, including Isolation Forest and One-Class SVM, were evaluated together. The results highlighted the value of adaptive learning-based approaches in flexibility, detection quality, and adaptation to emerging fraud scenarios.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
