206 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (Isolation Forest is a decision tree-based anomaly detection algorithm. Its core approach is based on the idea of isolating data points rather than modeling statistical distributions. The model assumes that anomalous observations are inherently easier to separate, or isolate, from the rest of the data.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
207 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (At each step, the algorithm randomly selects a feature and a threshold value for that feature, then recursively partitions the data into binary decision trees. Each tree, referred to as an iTree, represents the number of splits required to isolate an observation. The average isolation depth is calculated for each data point, and observations that can be isolated with fewer splits are identified as anomalies.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
208 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 583 0 R
/E (Anomalous observations can typically be isolated at higher levels of the tree with fewer splits.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 584 0 R
/E (Normal observations generally require more splits and are isolated at deeper levels of the tree.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
