<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 130 0 R
/E (Unlike conventional classification algorithms, One-Class SVM learns from a single class and therefore does not distinguish between multiple labeled categories in the traditional sense. Instead, it focuses on modeling the distribution of observations considered normal. In contrast to standard Support Vector Machine \(SVM\) approaches, it learns a decision surface that encloses the region occupied by normal data. Observations that fall outside this surface are treated as deviations from the expected data distribution and are classified as potential anomalies.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
