/E (Z-Score is a standard statistical method used to measure how far a value deviates from the expected behavior within its own distribution. In financial transaction data, the mean and standard deviation of transactions within a defined time window are calculated to obtain a Z-score for each transaction. This score provides a numerical indication of how strongly a transaction behaves as an outlier.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
